{
  "case_id": "2022-22-535",
  "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument, we'll continue argument, in Case 22-535, Department of Education versus Brown. Welcome back."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Are there any instances in which you would have procedural standing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: The -- this action has nothing to do with their right if they thought it was permissible to seek relief under the Education Act, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Counsel, I'm -- I'm sure I'm misreading the graphs on -- I'm looking at 247, 248. Didn't half the borrowers say they would not have any trouble paying their loans without regard to the forgiveness program?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I think, to the extent that there's concern here about how the standard could operate, at the very least, the Secretary made the requisite findings that these are financial harms that derive directly from and are a but-for result of the COVID pandemic."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Why is it fair?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I take your bottom-line answer to be everybody suffered in the pandemic, but different people got different benefits because they qualified under different programs, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I mean, Congress passed a statute that dealt with loan repayment for colleges, and it didn't pass a statute that dealt with loan repayment for lawn businesses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I think the right way to analyze that would be under arbitrary and capricious review because, as I've just explained, we think the statute tolerates some overbreadth. And so, at that point, you would want to look at the Secretary's justification for his action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: If --if it were party-specific relief and it went up to the court of appeals and the court of -- and you had sought an emergency injunction in the court of appeals and the court of appeals ruled against the government on that, would you then follow that in that circuit or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0002-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF J. MICHAEL CONNOLLY ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Connolly, has this Court ever held that the notice-and-comment provisions of the APA can establish -- are enough for standing in a --in a case like this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Except my biggest problem is you've shown me nothing to suggest that if they'd have to or will go under HEA, that they're going to deprive you of due process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But, Mr. Connolly, aren't you really fighting Congress on this one?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Connolly",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CONNOLLY: Because, when -- when Congress wrote the HEROES Act, the waivers and modifications have to actually be authorized by the Act. You can't just label something a waiver or modification and skip through negotiated rulemaking and notice-and-comment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Mr. Connolly, what are the limits of your theory?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Connolly",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CONNOLLY: Right. And -- and I would also point to negotiated rule -- the negotiated rulemaking statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: So, for purposes of standing, as distinct as to who can comment, because anyone can comment --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0004-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ninety percent of the borrowers covered by this plan make less than $75,000 a year, and the Secretary documented the extreme impacts that COVID had had on their financial affairs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-22-535",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
      "evidence_id": "ev-463a78cada97-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, General, Mr. Connolly. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
